<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pact of Brunnen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1315">1315</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Pact of Brunnen was an alliance concluded on 9 December 1315 at Brunnen, on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-lucerne">Lake Lucerne</a>, by Uri, Schwyz and Unterwalden, weeks after their victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> at Morgarten. Written in German, it renewed and extended their earlier league, forbidding any member to accept a new lord or make agreements with outsiders without the others' consent. It became a foundation of the Old Swiss Confederacy.</p></div>
